WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.170
Nicole: So, what motivates
bad and good actors?

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.480
Abraham: Bad Actors or threat actors
have malicious intent and are constantly

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.950
looking for ways to infiltrate an
organisations networks and systems.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:17.610
Nicole: Cyber criminals or black hat
hackers are the most common threat

00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:21.990
actors, and their aim is to exploit
human security vulnerabilities.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:27.590
Attacks may involve hacking into devices
to gain password details and stealing

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:32.400
or making data inaccessible to an
organisation by holding it to ransom.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.599
Financial gain is usually the motive,
and their weapons of choice are often

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.739
phishing attacks, ransomware, and malware.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:45.739
Abraham: Hacktivists are activist
groups or collectives who instead of

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.990
being motivated by purely financial
or personal gain, carry out 'attacks'

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:56.010
in support of ideological or political
causes and may target industries or

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.230
specific organisations, who don't
share their political views or causes.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.510
By disrupting organisations,
they feel that they can alert the

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:08.640
media and public to their cause,
but they do it by criminal means.

00:01:09.349 --> 00:01:14.830
One of the most well-known Hactivist
groups is Anonymous, known for their cyber

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:19.060
attacks on governments, corporations,
and the Church of Scientology.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.620
Nicole: Not only do threat
actors come from outside of an

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.190
organisation they also exist within.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:30.079
They may be former or current employees
who attempt to exploit vulnerabilities

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.520
using ransomware, malware and
hacking tools but with legitimate

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.570
access to networks and systems.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.470
Their motivation may be financial,
but it may also be for espionage

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.830
reasons or sabotage, or even just
for revenge, to get their own back,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.819
especially if they have been dismissed.

00:01:48.779 --> 00:01:53.020
Abraham: And then there are those who are
motivated by personal reasons, just to

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.160
have fun, create chaos or seek attention.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.020
These are threat actors known as
script kiddies, and are able to do a

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.950
lot of damage, just because they can!

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.180
Nicole: So, what about good
actors or white hat hackers?

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.789
Are they bad actors who
have seen the light?

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:12.630
For some this is actually true!

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:18.219
Check out Kevin Mitnick, who was
arrested in 1995 for black hat activities

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.749
by the FBI, now a trusted security
consultant with his own security company.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.430
Abraham: To know how to make
systems cyber secure and thwart

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.679
the hackers, cybersecurity
professionals must first think like

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.820
a hacker, then act like a hacker.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.699
But the difference is this is all done
with the permission and authorisation

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:42.289
of the system owner, in order to beat
the cyber criminals at their own game.

00:02:42.949 --> 00:02:46.530
They use all the tools a black
hat hacker would use but their

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.570
motivation is to be a force for good.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.359
Nicole: White hat hackers
or ethical hackers come in

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.949
a range of different forms.

00:02:54.309 --> 00:02:58.490
They perform roles of security
experts and analysts, penetration

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.140
testers and cybersecurity researchers.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.470
But their motivations are not just
about doing good, they can also

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.450
make a good living out of being
a white hat hacker or good actor.

00:03:09.929 --> 00:03:15.009
Afterall saving an organisation money by
improving its security can be worth a lot!

